    "public_api_change": "ADDITIVE",
    "schema_diff_summary": "fuzzy.rs has one test module named tests. Add the new test function at the end of that module, before its closing brace. Do not write a second mod tests. Do not add a second module with the same name. Change only the condition in digit_hump. Keep the let-else. let Some(previous) = index.checked_sub(1).and_then(|at| chars.get(at).copied()) else { return 0; }; The condition is one if. if previous.is_ascii_digit() && chars[index].is_ascii_alphabetic() { 8 } else { 0 }. Do not nest an if inside an if. Do not write if digit { if letter }. Do not touch fuzzy_match, score_one, boundary_bonus, gap_adjust, camel_bonus, next_index, or same_fold. The existing test a_digit_hump_adds_eight stays green. The test a_lower_letter_after_a_digit_adds_eight calls fuzzy_match of ab and a2b. The hit is Some with score 47 and positions 0 and 2. Branch from the current tip of main. base_sha records that tip at planning time. If main has moved, use the new tip. Keep the change under about 60 lines."
